# Parsed as inert text by sync-upstream.sh; never sourced or evaluated.
# KIND|regex matches a complete repository-relative path using Bash EREs.
# Rules must start with ^ and end with $. Escape literal dots with \.
# RECONCILE rules carry a required third field after a second separator:
# the make target that reconstructs downstream state. Patterns must not
# contain the | separator; use separate rules for alternatives.
#
# Rule kinds:
#   GENERATED  Machine-written outputs. Merge conflicts in these paths may be
#              resolved by running the generators; the candidate must still
#              verify clean before anything is published.
#   STAGE      Additional paths the sync may stage when the generators
#              rewrite them (side effects on hand-maintained inputs).
#              Conflicts in STAGE-only paths still stop the sync. The
#              staging set is GENERATED plus STAGE plus RECONCILE.
#   RECONCILE  Hand-maintained files whose conflicts are resolved by taking
#              the upstream side and then running the rule's named make
#              target to reconstruct downstream state (for example, the
#              pinned dependency versions in go.mod). RECONCILE rules carry
#              a REQUIRED third field: the make target name. Conflicts in
#              RECONCILE paths resolve before the generators run, and the
#              reconcile target must leave the file free of conflict
#              markers or the sync stops.

# Machine-written outputs.
GENERATED|^go\.sum$
GENERATED|^vendor/.*$
GENERATED|^pkg/mcp/testdata/[^/]*\.json$
GENERATED|^README\.md$
GENERATED|^docs/configuration\.md$

# Hand-maintained inputs reconstructed from the upstream side plus a make target.
RECONCILE|^go\.mod$|reconcile-go-mod
